			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Standardize naming conventions from Workspace/WebView to Workspace/Webview\n\nThis commit enforces consistent casing across the Cocoon extension host codebase, specifically changing instances of 'WorkSpace' to 'Workspace' and 'WebView' to 'Webview'. This alignment ensures the API surface matches VS Code's naming conventions (camelCase for `workspace` and `webview`) while maintaining internal architectural consistency.\n\nThe changes involve:\n- Renaming `WorkSpaceService` to `WorkspaceService` and updating all references.\n- Renaming `WebViewPanelService` to `WebviewPanelService` and updating all references.\n- Moving files like `WorkSpace.ts` to `Workspace.ts` and `WebViewPanel.ts` to `WebviewPanel.ts`.\n- Updating import paths and service registrations in `CocoonMain.ts`, `APIFactory.ts`, and `ServiceMapping.ts`.\n- Adjusting TypeConverter paths (e.g., `TypeConverter/WebView` to `TypeConverter/Webview`).\n- Renaming interfaces and variables (e.g., `WorkSpace` to `Workspace`, `WebViewPanel` to `WebviewPanel`).\n\nThese modifications improve code readability and align the TypeScript implementation with the expected VS Code extension API structure, reducing friction for developers migrating from the standard VS Code API.",
			"SHA": "327e4ad5b558df69f4c5ea44189c441d60958b46"
		},
